ADG Team,

We need to resolve RFI #020 regarding the jet bridge connection point elevations at gates C1-C12 as soon as possible. This is holding up our structural steel detailing for the gate area.

The issue: Boeing 737 MAX door sill height is 7'-6" AFF, while Airbus A321neo is 8'-2" AFF. The current design shows a fixed connection at 7'-10" which doesn't accommodate either aircraft optimally.

We see three options:
A) Design for 737 MAX (7'-6") and use the bridge's vertical adjustment for A321neo
B) Design for A321neo (8'-2") and use vertical adjustment for 737 MAX
C) Split the gates - C1-C6 for narrowbody (737), C7-C12 for A321neo

Option C has significant structural implications as it changes the floor elevation at the gate interface.

The Port's airline allocation plan would help us determine the right approach. Can you coordinate with the Port to get the gate assignment strategy?

We need a response by April 26th to maintain our steel fabrication schedule.

